# Opt29 (2026-10-29): (1) per-direction transport widths STRATA_PF_XPORT_BITS_X (card quant + host dequant of x) / STRATA_PF_XPORT_BITS_Y (host quant + card dequant
# of y), each overriding STRATA_PF_XPORT_BITS (not set in config S2); buffers are sized for the wider one. (2) STRATA_PF_GRP_FIT=1: the mapped routing-group table
# (ids | slot | src | bounds) is re-allocated for the prompt's chunk size instead of the --prefill size; the tgcu shim pulls every touched GPU-written mapped
# allocation whole after each synchronize, so a table sized for 3072-token chunks cost +1 ms per chunk-layer on prompts that run at 2048 (the 8K row loss of
# --prefill 3072). Falls back to the copies path on an allocation failure. Bit-exact (q23 vs config F: top-1 100 %, KL 0). Config S2 sets STRATA_PF_GRP_FIT=1.
